<Project>

  <Import Project="$([MSBuild]::GetPathOfFileAbove('Directory.Build.props', '$(MSBuildThisFileDirectory)../'))" />

  <!-- Everything under tests/: never packed, no XML docs. Each project is a test application on MSTest and
       Microsoft.Testing.Platform, which global.json selects for dotnet test. Coverage comes from the
       Microsoft.Testing.Extensions.CodeCoverage extension, with the settings in coverage.config beside this file, and
       eng/coverage-gate.cs holds it to its floor (AGENTS.md, Build and test). Tableau.Api.Aot is the exception: an app
       that CI publishes with native AOT, not a test, so it takes no MSTest. The name decides, because a project's own
       properties are not set yet when this file is read. -->
  <PropertyGroup>
    <IsPackable>false</IsPackable>
    <GenerateDocumentationFile>false</GenerateDocumentationFile>
    <TableauAotApplication>$([System.String]::Copy('$(MSBuildProjectName)').Equals('Tableau.Api.Aot'))</TableauAotApplication>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <PropertyGroup Condition="'$(TableauAotApplication)' != 'true'">
    <IsTestProject>true</IsTestProject>
    <OutputType>Exe</OutputType>
    <EnableMSTestRunner>true</EnableMSTestRunner>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <ItemGroup Condition="'$(TableauAotApplication)' != 'true'">
    <PackageReference Include="MSTest.TestFramework" />
    <PackageReference Include="MSTest.TestAdapter" />
    <PackageReference Include="MSTest.Analyzers" PrivateAssets="all" />
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.Testing.Extensions.CodeCoverage" />
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
